    "problem_statement": "The multiuser ostest suite needs the POSIX credential APIs added by the companion kernel change: setgroups()/getgroups()/initgroups() with a CONFIG_SCHED_NGROUPS/NGROUPS_MAX limit (initgroups must fail rather than silently truncate when membership exceeds the limit), and setresuid()/setresgid() for real/effective/saved UID and GID with correct privilege-drop ordering (setresgid requires euid==0, so dropping uid before gid must fail). On the old kernel these symbols do not exist (setresuid/setresgid are undeclared and unimplemented, and CONFIG_SCHED_NGROUPS is absent), so the new tests fail to build; after the kernel change they build and pass on sim:nsh.",
